  <entry>
    <id>https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/154.0/releasenotes/</id>
    <title type="html">Thunderbird 154.0</title>
    <author>
      <name>Thunderbird</name>
      <uri>https://www.thunderbird.net</uri>
    </author>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/154.0/releasenotes/"/>
    <updated>2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <published>2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00</published>

    <content type="html"><![CDATA[
      

  
  

  
    

    
      
        
        

        
          <h3>What’s New</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Preview functionality for attachments on macOS</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>CMS message with AuthEnvelopedData can be decrypted properly in Thunderbird</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Global search results can open in list view by default with new setting</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>"Copy To" folder context menu added for message/rfc822 attachments</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Optional system tray mode that hides Thunderbird when the last window closes</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Support for dragging message/rfc822 type MIME attachments to folder tree</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Microsoft Graph enabled for Microsoft 365</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        
          </ul>
        

        
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Remote content warnings appeared despite sender block exceptions being applied</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Collapsed saved-search folders did not deselect their subfolders</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Server-designated special folder flags could be removed until restart</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Messages could render excessive trailing blank lines</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Copying a message subject included the "Subject:" label in copied text</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Moving IMAP folders to Local Folders could delete messages after copy failures</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>7-bit clean unobtrusive signature payloads were unnecessarily base64 encoded</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>DisablePasswordReveal policy failed to prevent revealing saved passwords</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Account setup tried local-part usernames before full email addresses</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Read-only CardDAV address books were incorrectly treated as writable</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Autoscroll icon was missing directional arrows in scrollable messages</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Blank 1970-dated messages could appear from incomplete message file copies</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Opening drafts or templates with invalid quoted-printable data could crash Thunderbird</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could crash when inserting a message header into database cache</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>IMAP repeatedly notified for messages already read on another device</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Dragging EWS search folders to Trash caused Thunderbird to crash</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Folder compaction displayed incorrect disk space recovery estimates</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Custom OAuth settings for EWS account overwrote original account's settings</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could crash when going offline with an active IMAP IDLE connection</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could crash while running online mail search</p>
          
